This method is more advanced and can be less efficient for very long strings.

```javascript
function reverseString(str) {
  if (str === "") {
    return "";
  } else {
    return reverseString(str.substr(1)) + str.charAt(0);
  }
}

let str = "Hello, World!";
let reversedStr = reverseString(str);
console.log(reversedStr); // Outputs: "!dlroW ,olleH"
```

Each of these methods has its own use cases and performance characteristics, so you can choose the one that best fits your needs.

